                <pb facs="0012" n="2" sameAs="frus:frus1941v06/pg2"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00111 A.R.N.C./162: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Brazil</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Burdett</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio de
                                Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-01-22T11:00:00-03:00">January 22, 1941—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received January 22—10:18 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>43. For the Under Secretary from Fenwick. My telegram No. 42, January 21, 3 p.m.
                    Contrary to my expectations the Neutrality Committee <pb facs="0013" n="3"
                        xml:id="pg3"/> reconsidered the text of the Security Zone Convention and
                    eliminated from article III reference to warships making repairs and obtaining
                    fuel in neutral ports. [Fenwick.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Burdett</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
